{:edb/db-before-t 1789 :edb/db-after-t 1790 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535102 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:53:25.817Z" 13194139535102 true] [17592186175754 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2xy - x^2 - y^2$.\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x - y$, transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z)$. What is the function $f(z)$?" 13194139535102 false] [17592186175754 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 2xy - x^2 - y^2.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x - y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186175754 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= - (x - y)^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n$z = x - y$.\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 - \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 - \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1 - \\frac{dz}{dx} &= -z^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form\n\n$$\nz'(x) = f(z)\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = z^2 + 1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = z^2 + 1\n$$" 13194139535102 false] [17592186175754 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-(x-y)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x - y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 - \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} =  1 - \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  =  z^2 + 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = z^2 + 1.$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186175755 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}  = \\dfrac{1 - x - y}{x + y}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = 2x + C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186175755 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1 - x - y}{x + y}$.\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n$g(x,y) = 2x + C$,\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)$?" 13194139535102 false] [17592186175755 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= (1 - (x + y))/(x + y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dz}{dx} - 1 &= \\frac{1 - z}{z}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form\n\n$$\nz'(x) = f(z)\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{z}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz\\frac{dz}{dx} &= 1 \\\\\n∫zdz &= ∫dx \\\\\n\\frac{z^{2}}{2} &= x + K \\\\\nz^{2} &= 2x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = 2K$.\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+y)^2 = 2x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = (x+y)^2\n$$" 13194139535102 false] [17592186175755 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-(x+y)}{x+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{1-z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =x+K \\\\ {z}^{2} & =2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = 2K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+y)^2 = 2x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\ng(x,y) = (x+y)^2.\n$$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331185 13194139535102 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331192 13194139535102 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331199 13194139535102 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331206 13194139535102 true] [17592186175907 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331220 13194139535102 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331178 13194139535102 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331213 13194139535102 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331227 13194139535102 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331234 13194139535102 true] [17592186175908 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331241 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331179 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1089 "q-107815" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x+y}{3-2x-y}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|g(x,y)|=-\\frac{x+y}{3}+C\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1113 #uuid "a70f4011-4095-5c5c-9618-7d0bafab75e3" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331178 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x+y}{3-(2x+y)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2 & =\\frac{z}{3-z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6-z}{3-z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{3-z}{6-z})\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int (\\frac{z-3}{z-6})\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{3}{z-6}+1)\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ 3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|z-6|+z & =x+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+y-6|+2x+y & =x+K \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+y-6| & =-\\frac{x+y}{3}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{K}{3}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=2x+y-6.\n$$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331180 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331181 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331182 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331183 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331184 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1041 "selection" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331183 13194139535102 true] [17592186331179 1110 #uuid "573c3678-f514-54e8-affa-eef87ad08a37" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331180 1034 "2x+y-3" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331180 1111 #uuid "0640566c-2a53-5bfa-9000-3c75aababe7c" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331181 1034 "2x+y+3" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331181 1111 #uuid "b2259e1a-fd12-54bb-9b79-25dc3270bc7b" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331182 1034 "x+y-6" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331182 1111 #uuid "ad48cf59-082d-5094-a471-77cff00eb457" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331183 1034 "2x+y-6" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331183 1111 #uuid "82f4c438-bbc4-54f8-a631-f7b0e02e9a4d" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331184 1034 "-x-y+3" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331184 1111 #uuid "5ac0ad70-5f05-59b9-ae1a-f778f211c4d1" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331186 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1089 "q-108736" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}+6xy+3{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1113 #uuid "fec4fdaf-56a7-522b-8d95-ea2485a21ffa" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331185 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3(x+y)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3{z}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=3{z}^{2}+1.$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331187 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331188 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331189 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331190 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331191 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1041 "selection" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331188 13194139535102 true] [17592186331186 1110 #uuid "03e98113-d8bb-5253-a144-550249df0549" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331187 1034 "6{z}^{2}+2" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331187 1111 #uuid "a3e6e875-21f0-5db7-926f-b027db4d79ef" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331188 1034 "3{z}^{2}+1" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331188 1111 #uuid "812036a8-b2fd-5a87-ad19-5148886333bb" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331189 1034 "3{z}^{2}" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331189 1111 #uuid "12777a36-fe4e-5d4d-ab33-61327efc0292" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331190 1034 "3{z}^{2}-2" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331190 1111 #uuid "533b4fcb-59c7-564b-9bdc-f81850a3364e" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331191 1034 "6{z}^{2}-1" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331191 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 true] [17592186331191 1111 #uuid "63808a1f-fa0c-5112-ac0b-776a99647c0f" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331193 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1089 "q-108744" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={tan}^{2}⁡(4x+4y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=x+y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1113 #uuid "993f5c75-e412-5bbe-b9e0-a96c54f0d801" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331192 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={tan}^{2}⁡(4(x+y)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & ={tan}^{2}⁡(4z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEx