2186045465 13194139535102 true] [17592186331199 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{8x-12y+1}{12x-18y+3}.\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=2x-3y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331199 1113 #uuid "bd5f84f3-55db-5db3-a4c1-830365d71688" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331199 1145 "First, we factor the right-hand side of the given equation, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4(2x-3y)+1}{6(2x-3y)+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=2x-3y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2-3\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}(2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}(2-\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{4z+1}{6z+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2z+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=\\frac{1}{2z+1}.$" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331201 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331202 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331203 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331204 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331205 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1041 "selection" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331201 13194139535102 true] [17592186331200 1110 #uuid "b47bc8b2-5c24-5d43-b309-eb36e7977cab" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331201 1034 "\\frac{1}{2z+1}" 13194139535102 true] [17592186331201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535102 tr